Lab: Implement Map ADT Operations 

A map associates unique keys with values. In this lab, the map stores:

Key: integer
Value: string
Implementation: C++ unordered_map
Complete five functions:

Insert(key, value)
Remove(key)
Get(key)
Contains(key)
GetLength()

Program behavior

The first input is the number of operations. Each remaining line contains one operation.

Input command -	Behavior

insert key value	- Insert a new pair or update an existing key
remove key	- Remove the pair, if it exists
get key	- Print its value or null
contains key	- Print true or false
length	- Print the number of pairs

insert and remove do not produce output.

Example input
11
insert 5 apple
insert 6 banana
insert 10 grapefruit
get 5
get 7
contains 10
insert 6 orange
get 6
remove 10
contains 10
length

Expected output
apple
null
true
orange
false
2

Notice that:

insert 6 orange
updates the existing value for key 6. It does not create a duplicate key.

